cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these corpora, please cite them as below."
title: "Perch blind dictation corpora: 420 veterinary dictations and traps with Kokoro audio"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-21"
authors:
  - name: "Talcoe LLC"
type: dataset
# DOI pending. Zenodo mints it after the first release. Add it here as doi: and under identifiers.
identifiers:
  - type: url
    value: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/Talcoe/perch-vetdictation"
    description: "Hugging Face mirror"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/perchvet/perch-vetdictation"
url: "https://perch.talcoe.com"
abstract: >-
  Six blind corpora of veterinary dictation, 70 rows each (45 dictations and 25 traps),
  420 rows in all. Each dictation names drugs from a fixed formulary of 66 brand and
  generic names. Each trap is built to bait a system that guesses drug names from sound.
  Three Kokoro voices read every row, which gives 1,260 clips as FLAC. The rows were
  written by authors who never saw the matching code. Ships with ground truth for every
  row and a scoring rule that counts drugs recovered, drugs missed and false offers.
keywords:
  - veterinary
  - dictation
  - speech recognition
  - clinical scribe
  - drug names
  - benchmark
  - synthetic speech
